<p>Ehlinger's testing tells a similar story from a different angle. His 4.93-second 40 back in 2021 was well below average even by quarterback standards — see how that compares in our <a href="/nfl-quarterback-speed-2026-combine">2026 quarterback speed breakdown</a>, where this year's combine class averaged 4.60. Ehlinger was never sold as a speed threat; he's a bigger-bodied, physical passer who has bounced between three organizations trying to stick as a career backup.</p>
<div class="calc-cta">
<div class="calc-cta-label">Free Tool</div>
